From 2174440e63f4b08983128ff506c89a5afd11f695 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Workstream 09: run.sh tests the core in this tree [skip
 ci]

Patch 0001 is applied in this tree now (workstream 4's candidate with
workstream 09's core commits on it), so run.sh's last stage no longer
patches a temporary worktree: it checks that patch 0001 is applied,
then runs the host tests of the rules, the ABI and the program (default,
capacity-preview, custody-preview, both), clippy of the capacity
builds, and the kernel with core-patch-0001, which includes the rules
port's comparison with the kernel. results/core-tests.log replaces
patch-0001-tests.log. No SBF, LiteSVM, verifier test or keyed Node test.

run.sh (all stages, exit 0): kernel 43 (+4 abi), bridge10 28, workstream
10's adapter 17, core 1,811 tests, 0 failed. Workstream 4's
scripts/test-run-exit.py passes against it (2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
